{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"c6d11ac5-af7e-4db6-a229-221d8980e451","content":"## Build Failure Diagnosis\n\n### Solution Structure\n3 projects in the solution:\n- **Core.csproj** (GUID: `111...`) — Built successfully ✅\n- **Services.csproj** (GUID: `222...`) — **Failed** ❌\n- **Api.csproj** (GUID: `333...`) — Never compiled (cascading failure) ⚠️\n\n---\n\n### Root Cause (1 error, 3 manifestations)\n\n**`Services.csproj` is missing a `PackageReference` to `Newtonsoft.Json`**\n\nThe file `Services/UserService.cs` has:\n- `using Newtonsoft.Json;` (line 2)\n- `using Newtonsoft.Json.Linq;` (line 3)\n- Usage of `JObject` (line 22)\n\nBut the `Services.csproj` does not include the NuGet package. The compiler response file for Services contains only framework references — no `Newtonsoft.Json.dll`.\n\nMeanwhile, `Api.csproj` **does** reference `Newtonsoft.Json` v13.0.0.0 (resolved from the SDK path), confirming the package exists in the NuGet cache.\n\n---\n\n### Cascading Failure\n\n`Api.csproj` was never compiled because MSBuild skipped it after `Services` failed (Api depends on Services).\n\n---\n\n### Fix\n\nAdd the missing package reference to `Services/Services.csproj`:\n\n```xml\n<ItemGroup>\n  <PackageReference Include=\"Newtonsoft.Json\" Version=\"13.0.3\" />\n</ItemGroup>\n```\n\nOr run:\n```bash\ndotnet add Services/Services.csproj package Newtonsoft.Json\n```\n\nThis single fix should resolve all 3 `CS0246` errors and unblock the `Api` project build.","toolRequests":[],"interactionId":"7c668294-9421-40f8-974e-7a3484db87df","outputTokens":448,"requestId":"8002:2D75D9:3A2BBA:421922:6A56DB03"},"id":"de022227-19e8-40ef-bd8e-951d2f83ed63","timestamp":"2026-07-15T00:57:51.557Z","parentId":"09be0472-119e-4d17-b869-6d3fa4f83b2c"}
